## 🚀 Overview
A tiny, **production‑ready** C++ program that finds the **largest of three numbers**.  
- Clean separation: core logic → `utils::max_of_three`.  
- `main` handles I/O.  
- **Self‑contained tests** using `<cassert>` (no external framework).

---

## 📁 Project Structure
```
src/
│   main.cpp          ← entry point
│   utils.hpp         ← declaration
│   utils.cpp         ← implementation
test/
│   test_max.cpp      ← simple unit tests
CMakeLists.txt        ← build script
```

---

## 🛠️ Code

### `utils.hpp`
```cpp
#pragma once
#include <type_traits>

namespace utils {

/// Returns the greatest of three comparable values.
/// \tparam T must support operator<
/// \param a,b,c values to compare
/// \return max(a,b,c)
template <typename T>
requires std::totally_ordered<T>
inline T max_of_three(const T& a, const T& b, const T& c) {
    T max = a;
    if (b > max) max = b;
    if (c > max) max = c;
    return max;
}

} // namespace utils
```

### `utils.cpp`
```cpp
// No implementation needed – the function is fully defined in the header.
```

### `main.cpp`
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include "utils.hpp"

int main() {
    std::cout << "Enter three numbers (space separated): ";
    long long x, y, z;
    if (!(std::cin >> x >> y >> z)) {
        std::cerr << "Invalid input!\n";
        return 1;
    }

    std::cout << "Greatest number: " << utils::max_of_three(x, y, z) << '\n';
    return 0;
}
```

### `test_max.cpp`
```cpp
#include <cassert>
#include "utils.hpp"

int main() {
    // Integer tests
    assert(utils::max_of_three(1, 2, 3) == 3);
    assert(utils::max_of_three(-5, -2, -9) == -2);
    assert(utils::max_of_three(7, 7, 5) == 7);

    // Floating‑point tests
    assert(utils::max_of_three(1.2, 3.4, 2.2) == 3.4);
    assert(utils::max_of_three(-0.1, -0.5, -0.3) == -0.1);

    // Mixed type (all same type required by template)
    // static_assert fails if types differ – compile‑time safety.

    return 0; // success
}
```

### `CMakeLists.txt`
```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.20)
project(GreaterThanTwoNumbers LANGUAGES CXX)

set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)

add_library(utils utils.cpp utils.hpp)
add_executable(app src/main.cpp)
target_link_libraries(app PRIVATE utils)

add_executable(tests test/test_max.cpp)
target_link_libraries(tests PRIVATE utils)
```

---

## ✅ Key Takeaways
- **Template + concepts** give type‑safe, reusable logic.  
- Header‑only implementation keeps the library lightweight.  
- Simple `assert`‑based tests run with **no external dependencies**.  
- CMake script builds **app** and **tests** in one go.

Run:

```bash
mkdir build && cd build
cmake .. && cmake --build .
./app          # run program
./tests        # run unit tests (silently succeeds)
```

Happy coding! 🎉
